{
  "name": "projects-close-window-remove-shown",
  "description": "The page removes the project that its window shows: the first removal is kept by a modified tab and sends no call, and the second releases the project, removes it from the registry, relays the operation of the removal and reads the registry.",
  "replay": false,
  "reason": "The steps send the theme of the window and the window calls of a project (windowReady, projectFolder, projectOpen, projectShown, windowState and the calls that close the window and release or answer the removal of a project), which reach only a window, and the notices of the window reach only the listeners of a window; the Go producer runs only log and workspace without a window (docs/spec/cases/page-wire/README.md#producer-runs). The registry of the host lists the project after its remove call, as the stored registry of the test did; the Go producer does not build that state.",
